# WebApi (`ForensicsAnalyzer.WebApi`)

ASP.NET Core: `[ApiController]`, `[Route("api/[controller]")]`, `[Authorize]`, `[HasPermission(Permissions.X.Y)]`.

- Controllers only send MediatR requests and return HTTP results. No DbContext, no domain construction beyond mapping IDs.
- Auth, CORS, Swagger stay in `Program.cs` / existing middleware. New middleware or auth scheme = architecture-gate question.

```csharp
// ❌ BAD
public async Task<IActionResult> Create([FromBody] Case entity) { _db.Add(entity); await _db.SaveChangesAsync(); }

// ✅ GOOD
[HttpPost]
[HasPermission(Permissions.Artifacts.Create)]
public async Task<ActionResult<Guid>> Create(CreateArtifactCommand command)
    => Ok(await _mediator.Send(command));
```

Document new endpoints in `PROJECT_DOCUMENTATION.md` (API table) and `docs/features/`.
